            <ArticleTitle>Bronchodilators: implications for nursing practice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-52; quiz 54-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Beta2-adrenoreceptor agonists are the most widely prescribed bronchodilators and are used for symptomatic control and as 'rescue' medication for people with asthma and other chronic conditions affecting the airways. The authors describe the clinical uses, mechanism of action and potential side effects of these agents, emphasising the nurse's role in monitoring therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
